    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing though... there isn't a \"safe path\" anymore. everything is just so heavy and it feels like any change i make is just a temporary fix before i fall back into the same hole. it feels more like a logical conclusion than a \"drastic decision.\" like, if a machine is broken beyond repair and just causing constant friction and heat, why keep forcing it to run? why keep forcing myself to run when there's just no payoff at the end of it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
